  "section_notes": "S2 contains no sales stop and no bounded transition, so a model above 5% can keep selling indefinitely under regulator-set conditions, which protects Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 per 100,000 per model, which bites on Ember 8 (9.9) but not Hearth 10 (6.4). S3's six-year retrofit window and S4's 36-month suppression start both sit within the acceptable range and are favourable to Northwind and Halcyon respectively."
